// Wave 2 piece N: DamageModify E2E demo. Caster gains a 5-second
// window during which incoming damage is scaled to 50%. Lowers to
// AbilityProgram { effects: [EffectOp::DamageModify{duration_ticks: 50,
// multiplier_q8: 128}], stackings: [Some(StackingMode::Refresh)] }.
// The .sim verb writes damage_taken_mult_q8 +
// damage_taken_mult_expires_at_tick; ApplyDamage reads target's
// damage_taken_mult and scales bleed by mult_q8 / 256.0 before
// subtracting from hp.
//
// `stacking refresh` exercises Wave 1.5#3 stacking-mode lowering — on
// recast, the .sim's ApplyDamageModActivation overwrites
// damage_taken_mult_expires_at_tick wholesale (no max-with-existing),
// which IS refresh semantics. Registry-driven stacking dispatch is
// later infrastructure; the binding-check asserts the lowered slot
// matches the .sim's natural overwrite behavior.

ability Fortify {
    target: self
    cooldown: 8s

    damage_modify 0.5 5s stacking refresh [DEFENSE: 100]
}
